      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n**To see current offers or place your own offer on this property, please visit SherryFitz.ie and register for your mySherryFitz account**\n\n** Open View Friday Sept 11th 11am - 12 noon **\n\nSherry FitzGerald Carroll are delighted to bring No. 1 West Terrace, Parnell Park, Dundalk, Co. Louth to the market. This traditional red brick, end of terrace property provides an excellent opportunity for purchasers seeking a project with the potential to redesign a charming period home in a well-established location.\n\nOf particular interest, the property may be eligible for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, subject to the relevant T&C's, giving discerning purchasers an opportunity to restore this beautiful home. \n\nExtending to 55.5 sq.m. / 598 sq.ft. approx. the residence provides for an entrance hall, sitting room, dining room & kitchen at ground floor together with two bedrooms at first floor. An outhouse w.c. is located in the rear garden. Externally, the property is situated in a quiet cul du sac position adjacent an open green space and boasts an enclosed west-facing rear garden offering potential for future expansion (STP). \n\nLocated in Parnell Park, the property is within walking distance of Dundalk Town Centre where a wide range of shops, cafés, restaurants, leisure amenities, primary & secondary schools are located. Within the immediate vicinity there is plenty on offer including Dundalk Grammar School, Tesco Extra, Lidl, the Avenue Road Stores, Marshes Shopping Centre & Oriel Park. In addition, the residence is convenient to Dundalk Clarke Train Station and M1 Motorway Junction 16 making Dublin & Belfast city readily accessible and supports those commuting or operating on a hybrid working basis. \n\nNo. 1 West Terrace represents an excellent opportunity for builders, investors or owner-occupiers seeking a refurbishment project with significant potential.\n\nContact us on 0429332173 or info@sfcarroll.com to find out more."
      },
